    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But isn't it true that the majority's \"history and tradition\" test is also criticized by many legal scholars as being just as subjective? It feels like the model is saying the dissent is just expressing \"preference\" while treating the majority's specific historical interpretation as the objective legal standard. Are there any major scholarly arguments that suggest the majority's own reasoning is what's actually flawed?",
